course: dictionary
lesson: 15977
title: Big changes and upheaval
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An upheaval is a big, sudden change that shakes things up. It can leave people confused, worried or in a mess. Look at the words around it to find its meaning. «Moving to a new town was a huge upheaval for the family.» A huge move that unsettles everyone is a change that shakes things up, so upheaval means a big, sudden change.
explain: The clues often tell you the feeling. «The new baby brought upheaval to the house: there was no sleep and there were toys everywhere.» No sleep and toys everywhere show disorder, so upheaval means disorder and confusion. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Upheaval has a second meaning in geology, the study of rocks and the Earth. «The upheaval pushed the rocks up into a tall mountain range.» Here the word means a strong upward movement of the Earth's crust. Same word, different sense: the context tells you which meaning you need.
fact: An upheaval is a noun, so you can say «an upheaval» or «upheavals».
fact: «Upheaval» means a big, sudden change that causes confusion, disorder or worry.
fact: Upheavals can be family events, such as moving house, changing schools or a new baby.
fact: In history, revolutions and wars are called political upheavals.
fact: In geology, «upheaval» means a strong upward movement of the Earth's crust that pushes up land or rocks.
exercise: «Moving to a new town was a huge upheaval for the family.» What does upheaval mean here? | A small, tidy garden | A quiet, relaxing holiday | A type of tasty meal | *A big, sudden change that causes worry and confusion
exercise: «The new baby brought upheaval to the house, with no sleep and toys everywhere.» What clues show that upheaval means disorder? | *No sleep and toys everywhere | The house | The new baby | Brought
exercise: «The upheaval pushed the rocks up into a tall mountain range.» What does upheaval mean in geology? | A sudden fall of snow | A quiet walk in the hills | A way of cooking rocks | *A strong upward movement of the Earth's crust
test: «Changing schools in the middle of the year was a time of upheaval for Sam.» What does a time of upheaval mean? | A time of free holidays | *A time of big, unsettling change | A time for sleeping late | A time of calm and quiet
test: Which is the best example of upheaval in geology? | *Land pushed upward over many years to form mountains | Snow melting in spring | A cup of tea cooling on a table | A river flowing gently to the sea
exam: Which best describes upheaval? | *A big, sudden change that causes confusion, or a strong upward movement of the Earth's crust | A type of rainfall | Something that always stays the same | A small, quiet change
